{"hypotheses":[
  {"cause":"Unhandled exception during process startup (application-level crash, not OS signal)","detail":"exit_code=1 with no captured signal (signal= empty) points to an application-level fatal error rather than SIGSEGV/SIGABRT. In .NET this maps to an unhandled CLR exception propagating past Main(); in JVM to an uncaught exception on the main thread; in Go to a panic that exits via os.Exit(1). The process starts, hits a fatal path (missing config, failed dependency handshake, nil dereference during init), and terminates with code 1 before the container becomes healthy — triggering the BackOff loop (count=27).","anchored_facts":["process_crash","crashloop"],"confidence":0.62},
  {"cause":"Runtime initialization failure: heap/GC bootstrap or native interop error at container cold-start","detail":"exit_code=1 can be emitted by runtimes before the application layer is even reached — e.g., .NET CLR failing to JIT a P/Invoke binding, JVM hitting a native library load error (UnsatisfiedLinkError mapped to exit 1), or Go's runtime.throw() path when the environment is inconsistent (stack size limits, /proc constraints in the container). The consistent crash-loop without OOM and without a raw OS signal (no SIGSEGV/132/134/139) aligns with a deterministic runtime bootstrap failure that repeats on every restart.","anchored_facts":["process_crash","crashloop"],"confidence":0.45},
  {"cause":"Async/thread-pool starvation or deadlock during startup causing the process to hang then be killed, or to self-exit with code 1","detail":"Thread pool exhaustion in .NET (all ThreadPool threads blocked on sync-over-async) or a goroutine deadlock detected by the Go runtime both produce fatal exits without OS signals. If the container has a liveness/readiness probe with a short timeout, the probe kill would register as exit_code=1 (SIGTERM → exit 1) rather than SIGKILL. The repeated BackOff events (count=27) without any OOM indicator suggest the failure is deterministic and fast, consistent with a deadlock hit early in the startup path.","anchored_facts":["process_crash","crashloop"],"confidence":0.30}
]}

